# Verified false positives — do not remove without re-checking first.
#
# Trivy reports "Installed Version: 7.5.11" for `tar` in the built
# backend image, but that string exists NOWHERE in the image (checked:
# grepped the entire image filesystem for "7.5.11" -- zero matches, no
# package.json/lockfile bundled in the final runtime stage even has one).
# The real installed version, verified directly from
# node_modules/tar/package.json inside the actual running image, is
# 7.5.22 (pinned via backend/package.json `overrides`, per #220) --
# newer than every "fixed in" version these CVEs cite (7.5.18/19/21).
# Reproduced with a fresh --no-cache build AND a freshly re-downloaded
# Trivy vulnerability DB (2026-09-25) -- same wrong result both times.
# Looks like a Trivy detection bug specific to npm `overrides`-remapped
# packages, not a real vulnerability. Re-verify (rebuild --no-cache,
# grep the image, re-scan) before assuming this is still a false
# positive if these ever start looking different.
CVE-2026-59873
CVE-2026-59874
CVE-2026-73566
